Adaptations:
- Namespaced entry replacements; backend helpers are unexported within the module.
- Shared native kernel state remains external.
- Module references and RCU/workqueue drains for namespace lifetimes.
- No duplicate boot-time sysctl registration or SLAB_PANIC allocation.
- PID allocation and do_exit paths compiled with PID_NS helpers enabled.
- Namespace management/setns/procfs use the transplanted operations.
- SysV msg/sem/shm, POSIX mqueue, IPC sysctl and procfs backends transplanted.
- Host CONFIG_SYSVIPC stays disabled: SEM_UNDO and shm creator lists use a task side table.
- kernel_clone prepares shared undo state before native copy_process, installs before wakeup.
- Native ARM64 IPC syscall table slots replaced under stop_machine; compat table untouched.
- Message allocation uses kmalloc/kfree instead of persistent boot-time kmem_buckets.
- Explicit backend init/exit replaces boot initcalls; pre-activation user mqueue mounts rejected.
- Namespace construction failures clear/unmount mqueue mounts before freeing state.
- Target gate accepts the recorded canoe device/kernel and the two tested QEMU kernels.
- FUSE connection, cgroup-v1 pidlist, BPF iterator and pidfd namespace references restored.
- Perf retains native implementation through validated relocatable prologues; a side table owns child namespace references.
- Container reboot is routed to reboot_pid_ns; initial namespace keeps the native reboot handler.
- memfd namespace sysctl/policy restored; native file allocation and seals retained.
- Read-only entry preflight validates symbols, syscall/BPF pointer targets and their KCFI hashes before hooks.
- Activation pins the module until reboot; no automatic boot loader is installed.
